In .NET 10 (MAUI), `WindowSoftInputModeAdjust.Resize` was deprecated/removed because Android itself deprecated `SOFT_INPUT_ADJUST_RESIZE`. The recommended approach is now **edge-to-edge rendering with `WindowInsets` handling**.

## Solution

In your `Platforms/Android/MainActivity.cs`:

```csharp
using Android.Views;
using AndroidX.Core.View;
using Microsoft.Maui;

public class MainActivity : MauiAppCompatActivity
{
    protected override void OnCreate(Android.OS.Bundle? savedInstanceState)
    {
        base.OnCreate(savedInstanceState);

        // Enable edge-to-edge
        WindowCompat.SetDecorFitsSystemWindows(Window!, false);

        // Listen for keyboard (IME) insets and adjust padding
        ViewCompat.SetOnApplyWindowInsetsListener(Window!.DecorView, new InsetsListener());
    }

    private class InsetsListener : Java.Lang.Object, IOnApplyWindowInsetsListener
    {
        public WindowInsetsCompat OnApplyWindowInsets(Android.Views.View v, WindowInsetsCompat insets)
        {
            var imeInsets = insets.GetInsets(WindowInsetsCompat.Type.Ime());
            var systemBars = insets.GetInsets(WindowInsetsCompat.Type.SystemBars());

            // Apply bottom padding = max(keyboard, nav bar)
            v.SetPadding(
                systemBars.Left,
                systemBars.Top,
                systemBars.Right,
                Math.Max(imeInsets.Bottom, systemBars.Bottom));

            return insets;
        }
    }
}
```

## Why this works

- `SetDecorFitsSystemWindows(false)` tells Android your app handles insets itself (edge-to-edge mode).
- The `WindowInsetsCompat.Type.Ime()` inset reports the keyboard height.
- When the keyboard opens, the bottom padding grows, pushing your content (including the input bar) above it.

## XAML side

No special XAML is needed, but make sure your chat layout uses a structure like:

```xml
<Grid RowDefinitions="*, Auto">
    <CollectionView Grid.Row="0" ... />
    <Entry Grid.Row="1" Placeholder="Type a message..." />
</Grid>
```

The `Auto`-sized bottom row will naturally stay above the padded area.

## Alternative: `KeyboardAcceleratorPlatformEffect` (simpler but less control)

If you prefer a cross-platform approach, you can set in `MauiProgram.cs`:

```csharp
builder.ConfigureLifecycleEvents(events =>
{
    events.AddAndroid(android =>
    {
        android.OnCreate((activity, _) =>
        {
            activity.Window!.SetSoftInputMode(SoftInput.AdjustPan);
        });
    });
});
```

`AdjustPan` scrolls the focused view into sight without resizing the window. It works but may not resize your `CollectionView`, so messages could be hidden behind the keyboard.

**The `WindowInsets` approach is the proper .NET 10+ solution** and gives you full control over layout when the keyboard appears.
